<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>Barbatos.SecsGem.MaterialFlow</PackageId>
    <TargetFrameworks>$(BarbatosTargetFrameworks)</TargetFrameworks>
    <RootNamespace>Barbatos.SecsGem.MaterialFlow</RootNamespace>
    <PackageTags>secs;e87;e90;carrier;substrate;slotmap;wafer;fab300;materialflow</PackageTags>
    <Description>The join between SEMI E87 and SEMI E90 for .NET: turns a carrier's verified slot map into one tracked substrate per occupied slot, and forgets them again when the carrier is done. E87 says what the machine read and E90 says what it is tracking; neither standard says how one becomes the other, so this package makes one convention explicit and replaceable - the slot and substrate naming, what counts as an occupied slot, and whether a wafer goes back to the slot it came from. Depends on Barbatos.SecsGem.Carriers and Barbatos.SecsGem.Substrates, which stay independent of each other.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The only package in this repository that depends on two standards at once, which is the
         whole reason it exists: E87 must not depend on E90 or the other way round, so the join
         cannot live in either of them. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Barbatos.SecsGem.Carriers\Barbatos.SecsGem.Carriers.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Barbatos.SecsGem.Substrates\Barbatos.SecsGem.Substrates.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
